# interplay_session_dependencies: Work across FIFOs ordered only by barriers: child 1's blit fills a buffer, child 2's compute reads it (a barrier on child 1's stamp), and the root FIFO's render and copy wait for child 2 (a barrier on its stamp). The root FIFO is rung first and child 1 last, so each waits on the next. Then the chain the other way round, two tasks sharing it, and all four FIFOs chained the same way. At the end nothing has faulted: the fault state and each node. No display: nothing here reports the host.
